## Capitalization

The "m" in "members of Congress" is not capitalized

## Theoretical terms

`Interbranch representation` is a subset of `interbranch work` that is on behalf of a constituency.
We use them mostly interchangeably, but interbranch representation should be used whenever talking about work on behalf of a constituency.
Interbranch work should be used whenever discussing whether interbranch work is representative or not.

"Incentives for strategic behavior in the political environment" should be shortened to "incentives" or "strategic incentives", not "political environment", unless specifically talking about the political environment.

"higher-performing" rather than "higher quality" ---
In general, avoid discussing legislator "quality" since this is both normative and ambiguous.

## Empirical terms

"requests" is what legislators make of agencies.

"demands" or ____ are what constituents make of legislators.

## Use Periods in Acronyms

U.S. not US

## Two words, not one

policy work, not policywork

## Don't hyphenate prefixes

reelection not re-election

`preexisting` not pre-existing

## Don't hyphenate compound words

`supermajority` not super-majority

`antigovernment` not anti-government

`recordkeeping` not record-keeping

`followup` not follow-up

`email` not e-mail

`undercount` not under-count

`overpaid` not over-paid

`nonprofit` not non-profit


